NAME
	web_scan - web server vulnerability and configuration scanner.

DESCRIPTION
	Perform web vulnerability and security configuration analysis against
	HTTP/HTTPS services. When Nikto is installed, it runs a web scan to identify
	misconfigurations, outdated software, and known vulnerabilities. When Nikto
	is absent, it automatically uses the native Python HTTP security inspector
	to audit security headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options)
	and server exposure.

UNDERLYING TOOL
	nikto (with native HTTP security header inspector fallback)

EXECUTION
	nikto -h <target> -Tuning 123b -ask no
	(Fallback: native requests / urllib HTTP security header inspection)

USAGE
	use web_scan

MODULE OPTION
	target - target URL, hostname, or IP address.

COMMANDS
	show modules
		Display available modules.

	set target <url/host>
		Define the target URL or web host.

	run
		Execute the web scanning module.

EXAMPLE
	use web_scan
	set target http://127.0.0.1:8080
	run

OUTPUT
	Structured findings containing identified web vulnerabilities,
	missing security headers, and server banner details.

REQUIREMENTS
	nikto (optional); Python requests/urllib standard libraries used as fallback.

